From 7e9364f6cca54f3e88126d331cce352ed94d7bd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MedSphere Agent <agent@medsphere.local>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 16:34:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: unify app-wide language system with completeness gating
 (Task 0009, partial)

Core fix: closes the disconnection between the two existing language
mechanisms -- the top-nav LanguageSelector (23-locale frontend catalog,
updated the UI but only persisted to localStorage) and the Settings
Language panel (backend-persisted via the already-correct, self-only
PATCH /users/me/language, but never updated the rendered UI). Neither
restored a preference across devices.

- add isLocaleComplete()/enabledLocaleOptions to lib/i18n.ts: computed
  live from the actual catalog (every key in englishMessages must have
  a real override), not a hand-maintained flag. Measured finding: only
  en and ta had genuine 100% coverage; the other 21 locales (including
  all 3 RTL ones) silently fell back to English for registration text
  while still being exposed in the selector
- complete Urdu's translation in full (registration.* keys added,
  matching Tamil's coverage) so there is one genuine, complete,
  RTL-enabled locale to actually support -- not just a theoretical dir
  flag with no complete content behind it
- gate LanguageSelector to enabledLocaleOptions only; update the two
  pre-existing tests that encoded the old "expose all 23" behavior
- packages/i18n: add ENABLED_UI_LANGUAGES = [en, ta, ur] as the
  narrower "complete enough to be a whole-app UI preference" set,
  kept distinct from the broader SupportedLanguage set used for
  backend-generated system strings (hi/te/kn keep their existing
  backend translations for that separate, smaller purpose); narrow
  update-language.dto.ts's validator and the /localization/languages
  metadata endpoint to this set; add a ur.json placeholder (English
  fallback covers it, matching the service's existing fallback design)
- add preferredLanguage through the entire login chain: Prisma select
  (both password and Google login identity queries) -> LoginIdentity
  type -> response construction -> LoginResponseDto -> frontend
  AuthenticatedUser contract -- closes the "another device restores
  preference" gap, since nothing previously carried this value to the
  client at all
- LanguageProvider: implement the documented precedence (authenticated
  profile > local storage > browser locale > default), and make
  setLocale fire a best-effort, fire-and-forget PATCH to persist for
  authenticated users -- safe to call unconditionally from any page
  since the underlying route already no-ops on no session
- root layout reads the session server-side and passes it down as
  initialLocale
- SettingsWorkspace now calls useLanguage().setLocale() after a
  successful save, so choosing a language in Settings updates the live
  UI immediately instead of only taking effect after a future reload
  (direct fix for the core bug, with a dedicated regression test)
- add packages/i18n test infra (had none before) matching
  packages/logger's established build-then-node:test convention

Tests: 15 (i18n completeness/RTL) + 7 (language-provider precedence/
persistence) + 7 (packages/i18n enabled-set) + updated
language-selector (5) + settings-workspace (6, incl. 1 new) + 6 other
files' fixtures updated for the new required AuthenticatedUser field
(25 tests, all still passing, confirming zero regressions from the
type change) = 58 tests total, all passing.

No schema/migration change: preferredLanguage already existed as a
User column; only its exposure/validation surface changed.

TypeScript, ESLint, Prettier: clean across every changed file in
apps/web, apps/auth-service, and packages/i18n.

Explicitly NOT done in this pass (task scope vastly exceeds what a
single implementation session can respectably cover to production
quality): the full per-screen hardcoded-string audit beyond what was
directly touched; translating the remaining 20 locales' registration/
OTP/dashboard/navigation/inventory/reservation/settings/validation
copy; RTL layout-sensitive component behavior beyond the dir attribute
(navigation alignment, icon mirroring, dialogs, tables); notification-
content locale-awareness; validation/backend error-code-to-localized-
copy mapping; workstation-lock/re-authentication screen localization.
These remain genuinely incomplete and are reported as such rather than
claimed done.
